% Swiss banknote (Flury & Riedwyl 1988, Multivariate Statistics: A Practical Approach, Tables 1.1-1.2)
% Raw features (mm): Length, Left, Right, Bottom, Top, Diagonal
% Features: PCA of mean-centred raw measurements (no scaling), top-2 PCs (variance share 0.668 + 0.208)
% Axis sign fixed so that the largest-|value| entry of each axis is positive
% class: 1=genuine (rows 1-100), 2=counterfeit (rows 101-200), following the original source;
%   the uploaded Wolfram sample CSV had these two labels swapped (measurements identical row by row)
% N=200, d=2
@RELATION swiss_banknote_pca2

@ATTRIBUTE pc1 REAL
@ATTRIBUTE pc2 REAL
@ATTRIBUTE class {1,2}

